 9, Single J, or Pair of 10s against two opponents with 16 cards each is very risky; they will likely beat my lead, and I will be left with difficult singles and potentially only the Red Joker as re-entry, which is not enough to clear the hand reliably.\n\nReason: It is better to Pass on the King. The King is a high card, and using a 2 to beat it is a significant resource expenditure. By passing, I save my 2 and Red Joker to beat an Ace or 2 later, or to take control when it is more advantageous. Additionally, passing might allow the opponents to lead lower cards in the next round, giving me a better opportunity to sneak in my 9 or J or play the Pair of 10s effectively.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
